      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:lensing_concentrator",
      "title": "Lensing Concentrator",
      "text": "Lines a star up behind a mass and collects the light the mass bends together: an Einstein ring, made into power.$(br2)Generates power.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 3$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Works only at night under open sky. Choose the lens mass, its distance, and how closely the star is aligned behind it (u, in Einstein radii). The magnification is A = (u\u00b2 + 2)/(u\u221a(u\u00b2 + 4)) - huge as u \u2192 0, but the Einstein radius of a small, distant lens is so tiny that the aim's own jitter sets how close you can get."
    },
